    <Placemark>
      <name>Steps8 Foodbank</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Our food parcel programme specifically caters for low-income families.<br>To provide a maximum of three parcels in any six-month period (exceptions can apply, referrals to be negotiated on an individual basis).<br><br>Please complete our initial form of interest so that we can contact you with more information and to answer any queries.<br>https://www.steps8.co.uk/foodbank<br><br>We aim to provide nutritionally balanced emergency food-aid for people in crisis, identified and referred. (exceptions can apply, referrals to be negotiated on an individual basis).<br>To signpost customers to other agencies appropriate to their needs, such as: Citizens Advice Bureau, housing departments, adult and communities services, Age Concern, Sure Start, probation services and other relevant community projects.<br>We aim to bring communities together to end hunger and poverty in the UK by providing compassionate, practical help with dignity whilst challenging inequality of food poverty.<br><br>Food Allergens:<br>Please be advised that your food parcel may contain these ingredients; Milk, Eggs, Wheat, Soybean, Peanuts, Tree nuts, Fish & Shellfish.<br><br>Anderton Park School, B12 8BL - Monday after school<br><br>St Ambrose Church - Thursday 2pm onwards<br><br>[Dec 25]]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0F9D58-labelson</styleUrl>
      <Point>
