      <description><![CDATA[Warm hub without food offer<br><br>Opening hours<br><br>Monday drop in sessions.<br>Friday, 10am to 4pm<br><br>Community Day - a range of activities taking place every week, please see below for details.<br><br>11am – 1pm: Deaf Chat in the café area.<br><br>1pm – 3pm: Various activities every week including arts and crafts, dance, makeup and exercise classes.<br><br>2:30pm – 4pm: Let’s Chat group for hard of hearing people.<br><br>Please contact us to find out more about our Community Day or if you are interested in joining one of the groups.<br><br>Text/FaceTime/call Kim on 07561 682788<br>Email: community@bid.org.uk<br>https://www.bid.org.uk/services/birmingham-advice-support-service/<br><br>Services<br>Accessible entrance<br>Free Wi-Fi<br>Charging facilities for phones and other devices<br>Refreshments such as hot drinks, cordials, and biscuits<br>Toilets, including accessible toilets and baby-changing facilities<br><br>Deaf Cultural Centre,<br>Ladywood Road,<br>Birmingham,<br>B16 8SZ<br><br>[June 25]]]></description>
